cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RAGFuzz in research, evaluation, or teaching, cite the exact version or commit you used."
title: "RAGFuzz: A Local-First RAG Security Evaluation Workspace"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reed
    given-names: "Jonathan R."
repository-code: "https://github.com/JonathanRReed/RAGFuzz"
url: "https://jonathanrreed.com/projects/ragfuzz/"
version: 0.4.0
license: FSL-1.1-MIT
abstract: >-
  RAGFuzz is a local-first workspace for testing chat and retrieval-augmented
  generation systems against prompt injection, leakage, poisoning, retrieval
  conflict, grounding failures, context flooding, and related security risks.
  It records replayable cases and produces redacted HTML, Markdown, and JSON
  evidence for authorized local evaluation.
keywords:
  - RAG security
  - prompt injection
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - LLM evaluation
  - red teaming
